his is never added to a credit or debt figure. The IMF counts money the same way in every country, which can be wider than the country's own measure of money. The lines the IMF publishes for Switzerland leave up to 24.34% of broad money unplaced in the last two years, shown as its own row. Source: International Monetary Fund."}